<%- include('../partials/head') %>

<div class="pagehead">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>About the business</h1>
    <p>Who runs this shop and what it actually sells.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="section">
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <% if (placeholderCount > 0) { %>
      <div class="note note-pending">
        <h3>Business details pending</h3>
        <p>
          The licence holder has not yet supplied the trading history, staff and premises detail that belongs
          on this page. It is left empty rather than filled with invented background, because a page about a
          licensed firearms business that contains made up history is worse than no page at all.
        </p>
        <p>To complete it, the shop needs to supply: trading name and legal entity, the licence number and type, how long it has traded, the premises address, who runs it, and any trade body membership.</p>
      </div>
    <% } %>

    <h2>What is in the catalogue</h2>
    <p>
      <%= stats.total %> listings across <%= stats.modelCount %> Glock models, covering factory
      configurations, factory colored finishes, custom slide and grip work, optic ready builds, spare slides
      and drop in triggers. Prices run from $<%= money(stats.minPrice) %> to $<%= money(stats.maxPrice) %>.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
    <p>
      Every listing on this site is generated from the shop's own stock export. The caliber, barrel length,
      magazine capacity, SKU, price and availability shown on a product page are the values held in that
      record. Where a field is missing from the record, the product page leaves it out instead of filling it
      with a plausible number.
    </p>

    <h2>Marketing copy</h2>
    <p>
      The supplier export arrived with promotional descriptions attached. That copy made claims the shop
      cannot evidence, so none of it was published. Product pages carry the specification table and a factual
      one line summary until the shop writes descriptions it can stand behind.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site is not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It is not affiliated with Glock Ges.m.b.H. GLOCK is their registered trademark.</li>
      <li>It does not publish customer reviews or ratings, because none have been collected. No rating markup is emitted to search engines either.</li>
      <li>It does not process payments or complete a firearm sale online.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Use the <a href="/contact">contact form</a>. Business details, licence number and premises address appear in the footer of every page once confirmed.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<%- include('../partials/footer') %>
